[38;2;124;124;124mThese equivalences are well-known.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo the proof is:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m1. For a Kac-type compact quantum group, the scaling group is trivial, so $S = [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mR$ (the unitary antipode).[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m2. $R$ is a *-anti-automorphism of the C*-algebra with $h \circ R = h$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m3. Since $h$ is tracial (Kac type), $R$ is unitary on $L^2(A, h)$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m4. Therefore $\|S\| = \|R\| = 1$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m5. In particular, $\|S\| = 2$ is impossible.[0m

